# Every entry of msil-ld's built-in [mscorlib] table resolves through [mscorlib] on every runtime of the leg; an entry that is not mscorlib-safe fails the probe.
# Without references msil-ld binds the BCL types and members of its output
# through its built-in table (plan 5.11.7, Q10; D10 as amended for M21): the
# mscorlib-safe entries of llvm/include/llvm/CLI/BCLMembers.def, bound to
# mscorlib 4.0.0.0 b77a5c561934e089, which 'msil-ld --print-bcl-table'
# prints (plan 5.11.1). %msil_check_mscorlib_safe (plan 5.12.3;
# msil/utils/check-mscorlib-safe.py) writes an ILAsm probe that loads the
# token of every entry through [mscorlib], assembles it and runs it on every
# runtime the leg has (with the local runner the .NET Framework where it is
# installed, .NET 8 and .NET 10 where they are installed, and the leg's own
# .NET runtime; under msil_runner=wsl the leg's runtime inside WSL); a
# TypeLoadException or MissingMethodException fails it with the entry. The
# table it checked (DIR/table.txt) is Phase 2's (plan 5.11.7):
# M18's System.ValueType, the four owner types and Phase 1's five members
# (D10), and M20's Marshal::StringToHGlobalUni, EntryPointNotFoundException
# with its constructor, and System.Object; none of M21's NativeLibrary
# entries, which are Required but not mscorlib-safe. The second run shows
# that the probe catches an entry that is not safe: through [mscorlib],
# NativeLibrary::Load is a TypeLoadException on every runtime (the .NET
# mscorlib facade forwards no NativeLibrary, and the Framework has none;
# bcl-binding 2.2, 2.4), while System.ValueType still resolves. The third run
# shows that the probe loads the member, not only its type: Marshal exists
# through [mscorlib] on every runtime (the Framework defines it, the .NET
# facade forwards it), but it has no AllocHGlobal(int64) (only native int and
# int32 overloads), so that entry is a MissingMethodException everywhere; a
# probe that loaded only the owner type of a member entry would pass the
# first two runs and fail this one. Gate step 12 runs the script on all four
# runtimes of plan 5.11.7. Plan 5.11.7.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t
# RUN: %msil_check_mscorlib_safe --out %t/builtin > %t/builtin.out
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=SAFE%if msil-netfx && !msil-wsl %{,NETFX%}%if dotnet-runtime-8 && !msil-wsl %{,NET8%}%if dotnet-runtime-10 && !msil-wsl %{,NET10%}%if msil-wsl %{,WSL%} --input-file=%t/builtin.out --implicit-check-not=FAIL --implicit-check-not=failing
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TABLE --input-file=%t/builtin/table.txt --implicit-check-not=NativeLibrary
# RUN: count 14 < %t/builtin/table.txt
# RUN: not %msil_check_mscorlib_safe --out %t/unsafe --table %t/unsafe.txt > %t/unsafe.out 2> %t/unsafe.err
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=UNSAFE-OUT --input-file=%t/unsafe.out --implicit-check-not="2 of 2" --implicit-check-not="every entry resolves"
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=UNSAFE-ERR --input-file=%t/unsafe.err --implicit-check-not="entry 1"
# RUN: not %msil_check_mscorlib_safe --out %t/wrongsig --table %t/wrongsig.txt > %t/wrongsig.out 2> %t/wrongsig.err
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WRONGSIG-OUT --input-file=%t/wrongsig.out --implicit-check-not="2 of 2" --implicit-check-not="every entry resolves" --implicit-check-not=TypeLoadException
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WRONGSIG-ERR --input-file=%t/wrongsig.err --implicit-check-not="entry 1" --implicit-check-not=TypeLoadException
# SAFE:       {{^}}check-mscorlib-safe: 14 entries from msil-ld{{(\.exe)?}} --print-bcl-table{{$}}
# NETFX-DAG:  {{^}}check-mscorlib-safe: netfx (.NET Framework 4.{{.+}}): 14 of 14 entries resolve{{$}}
# NET8-DAG:   {{^}}check-mscorlib-safe: net8 (Microsoft.NETCore.App 8.{{.+}}): 14 of 14 entries resolve{{$}}
# NET10-DAG:  {{^}}check-mscorlib-safe: net10 (Microsoft.NETCore.App 10.{{.+}}): 14 of 14 entries resolve{{$}}
# WSL-DAG:    {{^}}check-mscorlib-safe: wsl-net{{[0-9]+}} ({{.+}}): 14 of 14 entries resolve{{$}}
# SAFE:       {{^}}check-mscorlib-safe: every entry resolves through [mscorlib] on {{.+}}{{$}}
# TABLE-DAG:  {{^}}type [mscorlib]System.ValueType{{$}}
# TABLE-DAG:  {{^}}type [mscorlib]System.Runtime.InteropServices.Marshal{{$}}
# TABLE-DAG:  {{^}}type [mscorlib]System.Environment{{$}}
# TABLE-DAG:  {{^}}type [mscorlib]System.Buffer{{$}}
# TABLE-DAG:  {{^}}type [mscorlib]System.Threading.Interlocked{{$}}
